# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles are executed inside Linux containers. With a
# Windows checkout under core.autocrlf=true they land in the build context with
# CRLF, and the container dies on `/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter` — a failure that
# never reproduces on a Linux clone, so it reads as a broken image rather than
# a line-ending problem. Pin them to LF regardless of platform.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
docker/nginx.conf        text eol=lf
docker/nginx.conf.template text eol=lf
docker/supervisord.conf  text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
.env.*.example  text eol=lf
